      "body": "## Pull Request Overview\n\nThis PR adds support for a new `Inconsistent` type provenance variant and implements a `consistent_join` operation for types, along with a new Dynamic Type projector feature.\n\n- Adds `Inconsistent` as a new type provenance variant throughout the type system\n- Implements `consistent_join` function that returns `Unknown(Inconsistent)` instead of failing when types can't be joined\n- Adds a new Dynamic Type projector (DynType) with keyboard shortcut and UI styling\n\n### Reviewed Changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 14 out of 14 changed files in this pull request and generated 10 comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Show a summary per file</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/language/term/Grammar.re | Adds `Inconsistent` variant to `type_provenance` type and its mapping function |\r\n| src/language/term/Typ.re | Adds `Inconsistent` to `cls` enum, implements `consistent_join` function, updates `join` with `~inconsistent` parameter |\r\n| src/language/term/TermBase.re | Adds `Inconsistent` case to pattern matching in `map_term` |\r\n| src/language/term/Equality.re | Adds equality handling for `Unknown(Inconsistent)` types |\r\n| src/haz3lcore/pretty/ExpToSegment.re | Adds `Inconsistent` cases to type precedence and parenthesization logic |\r\n| src/haz3lcore/projectors/ProjectorCore.re | Adds `DynType` variant to projector kinds enum and registration |\r\n| src/haz3lcore/projectors/ProjectorInit.re | Registers DynType projector in initialization module |\r\n| src/haz3lcore/projectors/implementations/DynTypeProj.re | New projector implementation that computes and displays dynamic types from runtime closures |\r\n| src/web/app/input/Shortcut.re | Adds Alt+D keyboard shortcut for Dynamic Type projector |\r\n| src/web/app/explainthis/ExplainThis.re | Adds `Inconsistent` to documentation lookup for unknown types |\r\n| src/web/www/style/projectors/proj-base.css | Imports the new dyntype projector stylesheet |\r\n| src/web/www/style/projectors/proj-dyntype.css | New CSS styling for Dynamic Type projector UI |\r\n| test/Test_Typ.re | Adds comprehensive test coverage for `consistent_join` functionality |\r\n| test/Test_Grammar.re | Adds `Inconsistent` case to type sampling function |\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udca1 <a href=\"/hazelgrove/hazel/new/dev/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.",
